From: fyDroidCreator (DC)
Subject: vulkan: expose VK_KHR_maintenance5 on Android 13 (zink requires it)

Mesa's Android allowlist (android-strict, the default) hides device
extensions newer than the platform API level, and lists VK_KHR_maintenance5
at API 35. fydroid builds for API 33, so every Vulkan driver hid it, while
zink has required it since "zink: use maintenance5" (f501f9453ad, in 26.2).
zink then rejected the device ("failed to detect features") and GL on zink
did not start: SurfaceFlinger aborted with "no suitable EGLConfig found" on
the NVIDIA dGPU (zink on NVK), and the same path serves AMD (zink on radv).

Allow it from API 33. The drivers that zink runs on implement it; the
Android 13 loader passes device extensions through unfiltered.

diff --git a/src/vulkan/util/vk_extensions.py b/src/vulkan/util/vk_extensions.py
index 75125d88855..f78823ee285 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/util/vk_extensions.py
+++ b/src/vulkan/util/vk_extensions.py
@@ -365,7 +365,7 @@ ALLOWED_ANDROID_VERSION = {
     "VK_KHR_index_type_uint8": 35,
     "VK_KHR_line_rasterization": 35,
     "VK_KHR_load_store_op_none": 35,
-    "VK_KHR_maintenance5": 35,
+    "VK_KHR_maintenance5": 33,
     "VK_KHR_maintenance6": 35,
     "VK_KHR_map_memory2": 35,
     "VK_KHR_ray_tracing_position_fetch": 35,
